<title>USA: U.S. lauds Russian-Chechen deal.</title>
<headline>U.S. lauds Russian-Chechen deal.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States on Tuesday welcomed a deal aimed at resuming a troop withdrawal from the embattled Chechen capital, Grozny.</p>
<p>&quot;That is a welcome development. We urge both sides to continue their dialogue aimed at reaching a political settlement&quot; of the 20-month conflict between Russian troops and Chechen rebels, State Department spokesman Glyn Davies said.</p>
<p>The commander of Russian troops in Chechnya, Vyacheslav Tikhomirov, and Chechen rebel chief-of-staff Aslan Mashadov signed the deal under which the troop withdrawal is to resume on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
